      "id": "end-to-end-digital-business-workflows-transforming-kyb-kyc-kys-via-eu-business-wallet-F665Dh",
      "sector": "finance",
      "title": "End-to-End Digital Business Workflows: Transforming KYB-KYC-KYS via EU Business Wallet",
      "summary": "Use Case: This end-to-end digital business workflow automates and secures high-assurance onboarding across the business lifecycle\n- Know Your Business (KYB): Foundation for obtaining the EBWOID and EUCC.\n- Know Your Customer (KYC): Financial-sector onboarding, including IBAN issuance.\n- Know Your Supplier (KYS): Supplier onboarding, including invoice submission.\n\nProblem: Manual corporate verification is slow, costly, and creates friction. Gathering complex corporate data to comply with EU \nregulations (AMLR, GwG, e-invoicing, etc.), conducting periodic reviews, and preventing invoice fraud are key pain points.\n\nValue: Dramatically reduces onboarding time and administrative effort while mitigating transaction risks. Issued once, reused across the EU, and shared through different channels.\n\nOrganizations: Bundesanzeiger (Identity Issuer), Deutsche Bank (IBAN Issuer/Verifier), Bosch (Holder/KYS Verifier), SBB (Supplier Holder/Invoice Issuer) and legal representatives (EUDI Wallet/authorized signatories).\n\nWallets: EU Business Wallets (Procivis/Spherity) securely store EBWOID, EUCC, Company Info, IBAN, and other attestations using OpenID4VCI/VP and SD-JWT standards.",
      "organizationName": "Robert Bosch GmbH",
